- content_for :title, "Address check"
.address-checks{style: "max-width: 980px;"}
  %h2 Address check
  %p.text-muted
    Saved addresses and upcoming trips that would send a driver, or work out a fare, wrong. Checked each morning; GCRPC I.T. gets an email when something new turns up. Fix each one from its link.
  - if @pins.any? && @served_bounds
    = render "map"
  - if @by_kind.values.all?(&:empty?)
    %p{style: "color: #0ca30c;"} Nothing to fix: every saved address is on the map, in the service area and near its town, and no upcoming trip is over #{AddressScan::TRIP_MILES} miles.
  - @by_kind.each do |kind, list|
    - next if list.empty?
    %h4{style: "margin-top: 22px;"}= "#{AddressScan::KINDS[kind]} (#{list.size})"
    %table.table.table-condensed
      %tbody
        - list.each do |f|
          %tr
            %td{style: "width: 52%;"}= f.label
            %td.text-muted= f.detail
            %td.text-muted= @providers[f.provider_id]
            %td
              - path = AddressScan.fix_path(f)
              - if path
                = link_to "Fix", path, target: "_blank"
